# Run individually using an HTTP client that preserves Cookie responses.
# Use a test account and do not commit real passwords or tokens.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@email = 20260001@bjtu.edu.cn
@oldPassword = Old12345!
@newPassword = New12345!
@csrfToken = replace_with_current_csrf_data_token

### 1. Get anonymous CSRF token; preserve the response Cookie.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf

### 2. Update csrfToken from step 1, then login with oldPassword.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "account": "{{email}}", "password": "{{oldPassword}}" }

### 3. Get NEW CSRF token after login replaces the session.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf

### 4. Update csrfToken from step 3. Success expires this login Cookie.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/me/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "oldPassword": "{{oldPassword}}", "newPassword": "{{newPassword}}" }

### 5. Expect 401: old login session is no longer valid.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 6. Get an anonymous CSRF token for re-login.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf

### 7. Update csrfToken from step 6, then login using newPassword.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "account": "{{email}}", "password": "{{newPassword}}" }
